.TH CATALIST 1 "November 2026" "v@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
catalist \- local-first anime and manga tracker for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B catalist
.br
.B catalist
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B catalist
tracks the anime you watch and the manga you read in two CSV files on your
computer. Run without arguments, it opens the terminal interface; with a
command, it works on the lists from the shell. It asks AniList's public API
to look up a title to add, to refresh a title's episode or chapter count
after it changes (and once a day for the titles being watched or read), to
find the ids titles lack, and to fetch covers, which it draws with sixel
graphics through img2sixel.
.PP
A \fITITLE\fR is named by its id on the provider or by words from its name,
in any case; \fBanime\fR or \fBmanga\fR in front looks in one list only.
When several titles match, a terminal is asked which one; otherwise they are
listed and the command fails. At a terminal, lists are tables; piped, they
are tab-separated lines. Every command takes \fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ls " [" \fIanime\fR | \fImanga\fR "] [" \fIWORDS\fR ...]
List titles, new releases first. \fB-s\fR, \fB--status\fR \fISTATUS\fR;
\fB--sort\fR \fBnew\fR|\fBupdated\fR|\fBrating\fR|\fBstatus\fR|\fBtitle\fR|\fBprogress\fR|\fBdate\fR;
\fB--reverse\fR; \fB-n\fR, \fB--limit\fR \fIN\fR. Piped, each line is: type,
id, title, status, rating, progress, total, new.
.TP
.BR show " " \fITITLE\fR
Show one title in full.
.TP
.BR add " " \fIanime\fR | \fImanga\fR " " \fITITLE\fR | \fIID\fR
Search AniList and add the match picked (\fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR takes the
first), or add by the provider's id. Takes the options of \fBset\fR.
.TP
.BR set " " \fITITLE\fR " " \fIOPTIONS\fR
Change a title: \fB-s\fR, \fB--status\fR \fISTATUS\fR (watching, completed,
on-hold, dropped, planned); \fB-r\fR, \fB--rating\fR \fIN\fR (0 to 10);
\fB-p\fR, \fB--progress\fR \fIN\fR, \fI+N\fR or \fI-N\fR; \fB-t\fR,
\fB--total\fR \fIN\fR; \fB--volumes\fR \fIN\fR; \fB--rewatched\fR \fIN\fR.
Prints what changed. Also \fBedit\fR.
.TP
.BR next " " \fITITLE\fR
One more episode or chapter (\fB-n\fR, \fB--by\fR \fIN\fR for more).
.TP
.BR rm " " \fITITLE\fR
Remove a title, after asking (\fB-y\fR, \fB--yes\fR skips the question,
and is needed when nobody can be asked). Also \fBremove\fR, \fBdelete\fR.
.TP
.BR search " " \fIanime\fR | \fImanga\fR " " \fIWORDS\fR ...
Search AniList and show the matches, marking those already tracked.
.TP
.BR provider " [" \fIanilist\fR | \fImal\fR ]
Show or choose the provider, the site whose ids are shown and accepted.
.TP
.BR import " " \fIFILE.xml\fR...
Add the titles of MyAnimeList XML exports. A title already in the catalogue
keeps its score, progress and dates. All files are read before
anything is added, so a bad file changes nothing.
.TP
.BR export " " \fIanime\fR | \fImanga\fR
Print that list as MyAnimeList XML, which the import pages of MyAnimeList
and AniList read. Titles without a MyAnimeList id are left out and counted
on standard error.
.TP
.BR help " [" \fICOMMAND\fR "], " -h ", " --help
Print the commands, or one command's options.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print the version.
.SH TABS
.TP
.B 1 Anime, 2 Manga
Left, the filters by status and by rating from 10 to 0 with their counts,
and a stats card (days spent, mean score, episodes or chapters, rewatches,
volumes for manga, a bar of the statuses); in the middle, the sortable list
with a New column of released episodes or chapters not yet seen; right, the
cover, then the details and tracking cards.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1 2 Tab
Switch tab.
.TP
.B j k g G h l
Move, jump, and change pane.
.TP
.B + - P S R
Progress, next status, one star more.
.TP
.B e Enter
Open the details card. There, \fBj\fR and \fBk\fR pick a field (status,
rating, progress, total, volumes for manga, rewatches), \fBh\fR and \fBl\fR
change it by one, and \fBe\fR or \fBEnter\fR types a number.
.TP
.B n u c t s r p
Sort by new releases (the default), last updated, date, title, status,
rating or progress; again to reverse.
.TP
.B / a d
Filter by title, add a title, delete (asks first).
.TP
.B q
Quit. Changes are saved as they are made.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/anime.csv, manga.csv
The catalogue.
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/settings
The provider, and the day missing ids were last looked up.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CATALIST_DATA_DIR
Use this directory instead of ~/.config/catalist.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
When set, the catalogue is kept in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/catalist.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, output has no colours.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the work failed (a file could not be read or saved, no
title matched, AniList could not be reached), 2 when the command line is
wrong.
.SH AUTHORS
McKaigne <https://github.com/McKaigne/Catalist>
